bic_trace_step.reason:
In `sco_sock_connect()`, the socket state and type checks are performed before acquiring the socket lock:

c
	if (sk->sk_state != BT_OPEN && sk->sk_state != BT_BOUND)
		return -EBADFD;

	if (sk->sk_type != SOCK_SEQPACKET)
		return -EINVAL;
...
	lock_sock(sk);


Because `lock_sock(sk)` is called after these checks, concurrent connection requests can bypass the state validation, leading to a race condition.
